    "en": [
      {
        "paragraph": 1,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "O King girded with might, great is Thy Name in might, Thine is an arm with might.",
            "page_start": true
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/1"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 1,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King is clothed in vestments of vengeance on the day of vengeance, He requites His enemies to their bosom.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/2"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 1,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King is clothed in majesty, He dries the seas and subdues the pride of rivers.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/3"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 2,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King with ten vestments has girded Himself among holy ones, God, who is adored in the council of the holy, is holy.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/4"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King who dwells in light, who wears light like a robe, will issue our verdict as if it were light.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/5"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King has girded Himself with strength, His right hand shows strength while man has no strength.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/6"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King is clothed in righteousness and sanctified through righteousness. Thine, O Lord, is righteousness.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/7"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "This King splendid in His clothing with a helmet of salvation upon His head, God is seated on His holy throne.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/8"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King whose vestments are crimson when He treads down renegades and lowers the spirit of princes.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/9"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King whose cloak is like purified snow, is pure and in purity purifies those who purify their work to triumph.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/10"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King is draped in zeal, He is enflamed with zeal, He carries Himself high, like a warrior does He arouse zeal.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/11"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King — all the ends of the earth bow down to the King over all the earth when He comes to judge the earth.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/12"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The King, on the day when He rises for ever, every creature will tremble before Him, lofty and exalted and eternal.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/13"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s99",
            "printed_page": "35",
            "text": "The",
            "page_start": false
          },
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "King, who rules the world in His might, mountains quake before His majesty and jump like rams before His rebuke.",
            "page_start": true
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/14"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King, awe-inspiring to the kings of the earth, the earth is surely quaking before Him who dwells above the Cherubim, the earth trembles.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/15"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King, who has the strength to bear Him? For He bears all with strength and to the weary does He grant strength.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/16"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King, when He rises to give judgment on the day of judgment, to judge the proud in judgment.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/17"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King searches out the secret of those who go deep to conceal a plan in the depths, and He reveals and exposes the things that are deep.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/18"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "O King, command that the haughty tyrants should be hemmed in from every side by the fury of the tempest.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/19"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King assembles the kings of the earth when He fulfils in the storm the prophesy of Duma, then will He reckon with the host of the summit.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/20"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King, high and exalted in judgment, the might of the King loves judgment, the foundation of His throne is justice and judgment.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/21"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King is the just Judge, justice walks before Him, to plead for those who strive for justice.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/22"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King mighty in dominion, His throne is suspended above, His realm prevails over all.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/23"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King makes the earth quake with His glance, He shakes the foundations with His glance, over all there roams His glance.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/24"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 3,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King searches every creature, and all that he may do both below and above.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/25"
      },
      {
        "paragraph": 4,
        "fragments": [
          {
            "scan": "s101",
            "printed_page": "36",
            "text": "The King is God of eternity, the eternal people has crowned Him. The Lord rules unto eternity, the Holy One.",
            "page_start": false
          }
        ],
        "reference_unit": "stanza",
        "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_azur_gevurah/26"
      }
    ]
  },
